WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.867
There soon

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.167
could be

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.702
another South Carolina Republican.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.036
In addition

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.871
to Nikki Haley seeking the 2024

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.072
presidential nomination,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.773
Tim Scott,

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.041
the party's only black senator,

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.542
may launch his own campaign.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.143
He's kicked off

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.011
what his team is calling

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.712
a national listening tour

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.414
and is expected to speak next week

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.516
in early primary state of Iowa.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.517
Just last night,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.518
he was keynote speaker

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.086
at an event in Charleston

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:20.487
Our Gary

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.554
Tuchman was also there

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.490
and talked with voters

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.192
plus a packed ballroom

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.660
with many of South Carolina's

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.763
Republican movers and shakers.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.398
I'm retired. I used to be a banker.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.133
I made other people rich.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.200
This is the city

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.536
and county of Charleston, South Carolina.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.008
The occasion,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:42.809
the fifth annual

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.511
Black History Month banquet

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.546
sponsored by the county Republican Party.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.281
The keynote speaker

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.916
South Carolina Republican U.S.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.452
Senator Tim Scott. My story

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.622
is the American story.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.123
And Scott's story

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.292
could soon include running for president.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.127
I am running for president

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.396
of the United States of America.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:04.731
His fellow

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:05.965
South Carolinian, former

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.568
Governor Nikki Haley, already is.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.603
These Republicans in the Palmetto State

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.805
are enjoying the attention.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.840
And we were definitely a Trump state.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.874
And and

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.076
I think people still have

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.877
a great deal of feeling for him.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.345
But then there's a baby, Nikki.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.880
She decided she's going to run

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.582
and there's a lot of passion

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.516
for her, too.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.185
Larry Karofsky is a Republican,

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.820
Charleston County Council member.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.054
Well, it makes you feel pride

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.922
because both of them

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.457
are legitimate contenders.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.357
And you could imagine

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.393
either them being president.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.328
And indeed, a number of Republicans

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.329
we talk to here

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.263
are ready to commit

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.132
to one of their fellow South Carolinians.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.366
I love Tim Scott.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.234
I just feel like

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.436
he's got our best interests at heart.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.537
That's true,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.772
but not necessarily

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.073
on the top of the ticket.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.975
If you could set your own ticket,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.343
who would you vote for for president of

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.413
the Santos and Haley

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.249
would be vice president

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.283
or to Santos.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.552
And Tim Scott would be vice president.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.787
My suspicion

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.288
is that the one that will be

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.591
electable will be the.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.458
But Mark Knapp,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.993
a lifelong Charles Etonian,

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.962
still thinks Donald Trump can win

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.597
and is ready to vote for him again.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.965
I don't know if Nikki's really got

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.701
what it takes to deal with the swamp.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:16.569
What about Tim Scott

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.237
if he announces he's

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.204
running for president?

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.839
I like Tim a lot,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.108
but I haven't seen the demeanor.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.543
I think it's going to take

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.044
some wrestles

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.780
with little scalawags in Washington.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.649
There are some Democrats

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.184
who came to the scale to celebrate

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:32.552
Black History Month,

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.486
but most everyone else

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.287
we talked to did

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.189
vote for Donald Trump twice

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:36.823
However,

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.190
we met

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:37.857
quite a few

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.059
who are looking for a fresh face.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.194
Wouldn't you vote for Trump again?

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.063
Trump is divisive.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:44.998
He is.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:47.033
He continues to play

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.601
divisive politics cards

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.403
and he hasn't grown up since.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.804
I don't think I'm on the side

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.907
of leaning towards where we've been.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.508
I'm more focused on leaders

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.210
of presenting new opportunities

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.444
and where we could go from here.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.046
Does that mean that you're not leaning

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.148
towards voting for Donald Trump?

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.484
That's that would be my personal

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.618
preference, yes.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.487
Not surprisingly, at this early stage,

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.289
the majority of people we talked to say

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.123
they are not sure who

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.191
they will vote for yet.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.426
I've been a Republican since 1988

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.361
and I was a freshman in college

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.031
so I am very dedicated to the party.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.232
But you don't know which Republican

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.301
you like just yet to sound.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:21.734
And that's

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.802
what the chair of this county's

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:23.636
Republican Party,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.805
Maurice Washington, likes to hear.

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.806
He wants this campaign

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:29.676
to be a competition, not a coronation.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.079
This is not going to be this part to see

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.415
and allow the former president to

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.149
walk through

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.053
Gary joins us now from Charleston.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.187
During Senator Scott

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:41.921
speech, did

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.390
he raise the possibility of running

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.926
Senator Scott to not mention

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:47.827
the presidential race

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.861
during a speech, Anderson,

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.396
but before the speech,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.931
he held a short session

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.467
with journalists, local journalists,

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.168
not admitted

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.502
were the national journalists.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.003
A reporter

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.104
from The Post and Courier,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.472
which is the daily newspaper here

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.140
in Charleston, asked the question.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.142
Will he endorse Nikki Haley?

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.978
His response to her was, quote.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.346
Next question.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.480
Also, the paper says

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.681
a question was asked to him

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:09.816
what would lead him

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.551
to going into the presidential race?

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.386
And his answer to that was, quote,

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.255
I'm not going to dodge your question,

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.690
but I'm also not going to answer it.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.424
There you are.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.059
Which is an answer in and of itself.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.094
Gary Tuchman, appreciate it.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:21.461
Thank you.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.095
Perspective now

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:22.562
from former

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.663
Republican Congressman Adam

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.764
Kinzinger, who's now a CNN

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.299
senior political commentator.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.300
So it certainly seems like

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:27.934
some Republicans

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:28.635
are ready to move on

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:29.502
from the former president.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.870
Do you think they actually want to move

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.305
on from Trumpism?

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:34.974
Well, that's a good question.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:35.775
And, you know,

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.676
I think what's

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:37.810
what's interesting right

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.045
now, so Nikki Haley

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:39.912
and by the way,

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.648
I'm actually personally at Tim Scott's

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.815
and I know him personally.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.516
He's a good man.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.051
But Nikki Haley,

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.853
she has an opportunity

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.087
to distinguish herself.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.023
Let's just take the issue of Ukraine.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:50.356
You know,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.191
Donald Trump has been very clear.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.661
He would cut off aid to Ukraine.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.995
Ron DeSantis really

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.298
hasn't said anything about Ukraine.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.966
And Nikki Haley could be.

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:00.466
Keep in mind,

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.468
most Republicans still support us

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.437
supporting Ukraine in that war.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.472
But she's kind of avoided that issue.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.107
She's going out of her way

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.542
to not distinguish herself

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.343
from Donald Trump.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.512
And I personally think that means a

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.813
she may be just making

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.481
a play for vice president.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.949
But the other thing be

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.385
I think it means that she's

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.621
not, I think missing the opportunity

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.789
to be different

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.058
because you have to distinguish herself

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:25.758
from Trumpism.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.126
So I think there's to be a lot of people

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.695
that in the Republican Party

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.997
still a bit like Trump or Trumpism.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.498
But I think there's a real opportunity

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.900
for the person to come forward

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.268
and present an optimistic,

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:36.736
hopeful scenario for the future.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.071
I mean, how tarnished

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.073
is she by her association

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.074
with the former president?

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.008
I mean, when

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:45.578
you know when the back in 2015 2016

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.513
she was supporting Marco Rubio.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.648
She was, you know,

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:50.283
saying some

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.884
very tough things about

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.386
then candidate Donald Trump.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:53.820
Obviously,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.556
she went to work for him ultimately.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:56.756
Yeah.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.323
I mean that's like

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.592
99% of Republicans out there

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.526
have that sense.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.895
And so I think in her case,

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.264
I think what's done

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.133
damage to her when it comes to Trump

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.968
is the fact that she has been for him

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:09.702
and against him

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:10.470
then for him

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.071
then against them wasn't going to run

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.005
and then it's now running.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.375
So though that like Donald Trump,

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.110
they already don't trust her.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.878
Those who don't like Donald Trump don't

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.012
trust her.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:20.913
She has an opportunity

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:21.814
to distinguish herself

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.216
as far as being involved

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.450
in the administration.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.818
She actually did a really good job,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.387
I think, as U.N. ambassador.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.454
So I don't think being in

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.622
the administration

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:30.990
is necessarily going to taint her.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.225
It's been her Yes.

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:34.093
And knows hot and cold on Donald Trump.

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.461
How formidable,

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.329
formidable do you think

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.130
Tim Scott would be?

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.632
I look, I'll tell you,

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:39.932
since

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.301
I've since I even met Tim Scott in 2011,

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.970
I was elected with him in the house.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.071
I always had in my mind,

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.539
this guy is at least going

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:48.274
to make a solid run for the presidency

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.308
and probably be president.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.844
There is most people may know his name.

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.479
They don't know his story.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:55.615
Once his story gets out there,

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:57.016
it's really breathtaking.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.951
His whole life is breathtaking.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.854
And I think he's always been my kind of

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:02.388
dark horse

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.589
candidate in this race

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:04.424
that I think

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.725
nobody was talking about

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.260
until fairly recently.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:07.927
But I see him

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.829
as not not a great comparison,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:10.630
but kind of Bill

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:11.764
Clinton in 92

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:12.932
who came out of nowhere

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:15.468
and ended up rocketing to the top.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:17.737
There already I mean, Nikki Haley,

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:20.773
Tim Scott, Mike Pompeo, I mean, Bolton

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:22.608
it seems like there's already

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:25.845
a fair number of people, you know, in in

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:27.380
getting close

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.282
to running in one form or another.

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:30.416
It seems like there's going to be

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:31.651
I mean do we risk.

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.586
Is there the risk of a

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:34.954
you know of a huge field

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.590
that then benefits the former president?

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:39.559
There's a huge risk.

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:42.028
Huge risk. Just like 2016 happen.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.629
It really could happen again now

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.731
and it's a big worry for Republicans.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.033
Adam Kinzinger, I appreciate your time.

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:47.767
Thanks very much.

